wasi-libc (wasi-sdk-34) now ships native wasm32-wasip3 objects, so bootstrap's
wasip2 fallback -- and the assert guarding it -- must go. rust's own comment
says exactly this: "Once wasi-libc supports wasip3 this should be deleted and
the native objects should be used."

Left in place, the assert aborts the build:

    thread 'main' panicked at src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/compile.rs:445:13:
    wasip3 support is in wasi-libc, this should be updated now

Verified against wasi-libc 34: share/wasi-sysroot/lib/wasm32-wasip3/ carries
libc.a, crt1-command.o, crt1-reactor.o and eh/ -- every object this code path
copies -- with the same 71-file layout as wasip1 and wasip2.

Drop when upstream rust removes the special case itself.
